{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 30 (S4 chapter 3): a march home. The player lands on the western beach with only the Shaper, five wardens and five settlers; the old Hearth stands empty (nobody near it) on the northeastern plateau, sunk in a pit of black water so a Shaper who falls on the road cannot respawn and skip the march. Only the Shaper reaching the gate stones raises it (area trigger unit shaper, so no other unit can wake it early), and three old keepers (defensive wardens) come out of it then. If she has not arrived by 600 s the Hearth rises alone with the three keepers (time trigger until 0; the gate trigger still adds three more when she arrives), so a fallen Shaper cannot soft lock the level and the Hearth is not left bare to the 600 s raids. Pursuers (tribe 1, whose camp is on an island to the south, so they can never be wiped out early) land behind the band every 60 s and chase it to the gate (spawn plus fresh raid, until the reach stage), and a band from the Oath Stone cuts the road at the ford. Stages: bring the Shaper to the gate (reach); gain twenty four followers (fromStage); cut down eighteen pursuers (kill, tribe 1): two bands of six march on the Hearth when the stage opens (ridge and ford, staggered) and four more come every 60 s from 600 s until done, so a strong player ends it on the fight, not on a clock; pray at the Oath Stone (dormant until then, held by tribe 1, six posted guards plus sixteen keepers, four worshippers for 40 s under its ward strike); that wakes the old road ley at the middle plateau, and the player holds both stones at once for 210 s (hold n 2) while pursuers land on the beach (three at once, then every 75 s from 840 s) and pray at the ley (keepRaiders keeps them kneeling; before it wakes they stand on the beach). The bot loses the ley and retakes it in the bot runs. Not eliminateAll. Bot (hard, offsets 0 to 3) wins 23771 to 24321 (offset 1: 24084; stages at about 2000, 11000, 13750 and 16750), time limit 2520 s.",
